WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-GB

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:04.800
How can you learn new phrasal verbs
without being overwhelmed?

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:07.700
That's what Alejandra wants to find out.

00:00:07.700 --> 00:00:13.867
So my question is: How can I learn
new phrasal verbs without freaking out?

00:00:13.867 --> 00:00:17.833
That was Alejandra's question, but we want to hear from you.

00:00:17.833 --> 00:00:21.967
So send us your questions to our email address.

00:00:21.967 --> 00:00:26.500
Now let's get back to those tips for learning new phrasal verbs.

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:27.967
OK. Tip one.

00:00:27.967 --> 00:00:30.500
Context is key.

00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:36.300
You can learn new phrasal verbs in
context by watching films, the news,

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:39.533
listening to music.

00:00:39.533 --> 00:00:42.533
I've been stealing money from the company for years.

00:00:42.533 --> 00:00:45.967
Nobody's noticed, so I think I've got away with it.

00:00:45.967 --> 00:00:47.700
Oh, 'get away with',

00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:49.000
That's a useful one.

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:55.433
Tip two. When you learn a new phrasal
verb, don't forget to note it down.

00:00:55.433 --> 00:01:00.767
And remember to include your own example sentence.

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:10.600
Tip three. Don't forget the grammar.

00:01:10.600 --> 00:01:15.900
Find out if the phrasal verb you're learning needs an object.

00:01:15.900 --> 00:01:18.167
Is it direct or indirect?

00:01:18.167 --> 00:01:20.633
Can you separate the phrasal verb?

00:01:20.633 --> 00:01:25.233
These things will help you be able to use the phrasal verb.

00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:34.767
Tip four. Be selective.

00:01:34.767 --> 00:01:40.800
Learn phrasal verbs that are important
for your life and your interests,

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:43.667
and remember to personalise them.

00:01:43.667 --> 00:01:45.400
I have a Spanish exam coming up,

00:01:45.400 --> 00:01:49.467
so I'm going to read over my notes and brush up on my verbs.

00:01:49.467 --> 00:01:51.467
Use it or lose it.

00:01:51.467 --> 00:01:56.000
When you learn new phrasal verbs, use them when you're speaking,

00:01:56.000 --> 00:01:58.900
when you're writing, on social media.

00:01:58.900 --> 00:02:01.633
That way you'll be able to remember it.

00:02:01.633 --> 00:02:04.500
Hey Beth, my birthday's coming up soon.

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:06.067
Have you thought about my present?

00:02:06.067 --> 00:02:11.200
And one final tip. Remember, not all phrasal verbs are informal.

00:02:11.200 --> 00:02:15.633
You can use them in work and business contexts too.

00:02:15.633 --> 00:02:20.067
Right. We've had to bring forward the
meeting as there's lots of data to go over,

00:02:20.067 --> 00:02:23.600
but first I'll hand out the documents for you all to quickly look through.

00:02:23.600 --> 00:02:25.900
I'll set up another meeting for later in the week.

00:02:25.900 --> 00:02:27.033
That's all for now,

00:02:27.033 --> 00:02:32.300
but check below for more information
and I'll catch up with you very soon.

